# 詞： 睇怕

1. 佢今日遲到成個鐘，睇怕今晚又要加班補返啲工作。 (He was late by a whole hour today; I'm afraid he'll have to work overtime tonight to catch up on his work.)

2. 天空咁黑，仲有雷聲，睇怕一陣間會落大雨。 (The sky is so dark and there's thunder; it looks like it's going to rain heavily soon.)

3. 佢冇覆我電話又冇回覆訊息，睇怕佢仲嬲緊我。 (She hasn't answered my calls or replied to my messages; I'm afraid she's still angry with me.)

4. 呢間餐廳門口排晒長龍，睇怕要等成個鐘先有得食。 (There's a long queue outside this restaurant; I'm afraid we'll have to wait a whole hour before we can eat.)

5. 佢成日掛住打機唔溫書，睇怕今次考試會肥佬。 (He's always playing video games instead of studying; I'm afraid he'll fail this exam.)

6. 個颱風咁接近香港，睇怕聽日學校會停課。 (The typhoon is so close to Hong Kong; it looks like schools will be suspended tomorrow.)

7. 佢哋兩個已經三個月冇講嘢，睇怕呢段友誼好難挽救返。 (The two of them haven't spoken to each other for three months; I'm afraid this friendship is hard to salvage.)

8. 個樓盤咁貴，睇怕我哋呢啲打工仔一世都買唔起。 (The property prices are so high; I'm afraid ordinary workers like us will never be able to afford a home.)

9. 佢今日著到咁靚，睇怕今晚有重要約會。 (She's dressed so nicely today; I'm guessing she probably has an important date tonight.)

10. 架巴士咁耐都未嚟，睇怕我哋會遲到。 (The bus still hasn't come after so long; I'm afraid we're going to be late.) [end of text]


